# Cloudflare architecture rules

- Inspect relevant `wrangler.jsonc` bindings before editing runtime code.
- Durable Objects are strongly consistent per-key shards, not a global database.
- R2 stores raw/large objects; DOs store operational state and metadata.
- Queues are the distributed work frontier. Consumers must be idempotent and have bounded retries/DLQ strategy.
- KV is read-heavy eventual-consistency config/cache only.
- Browser Run is an escalation path after normal fetch/extraction quality checks.
- Preserve DomainCoordinatorDO and BrowserPoolDO coordination boundaries.
- Workers AI should not receive every raw result; cheap deterministic/relevance filters come first.
- Source discovery is federated and adapter-driven. No single search provider is total Internet coverage.
- Protect crawler against SSRF on initial URLs and redirects. Do not bypass CAPTCHA/login/private content.
- Keep dev, staging and production Cloudflare resources isolated.
- Run `wrangler types` after binding/config changes.
